WEBVTT

00:00:22.924 --> 00:00:26.691
I can't believe we
actually bought this thing.

00:00:26.724 --> 00:00:29.324
There's a reason charity
auctions have an open bar.

00:00:29.357 --> 00:00:31.257
Don't you think...

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.390
I don't know, it's kind of creepy?

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.457
It's okay.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:39.958
I'll keep you safe.

00:00:41.058 --> 00:00:43.390
Maybe you're the one i
ought to be scared of.

00:00:45.457 --> 00:00:48.557
Mmm. Let's go upstairs.

00:00:48.591 --> 00:00:51.691
Give me 10 minutes to lock up.

00:00:51.724 --> 00:00:53.591
Mmm.

00:00:53.624 --> 00:00:55.123
Make than one minute.

00:01:44.657 --> 00:01:47.958
If you don't hurry up, i'm
gonna start without you!

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:10.891
Babe, get the lights.
I can't see a thing.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:18.857
Do you smell something?

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:21.991
Ann?

00:02:24.657 --> 00:02:26.190
Ann?!

00:02:44.757 --> 00:02:47.357

...3-4-2-0.

00:02:48.424 --> 00:02:50.490
All right. You're in there.

00:02:50.524 --> 00:02:51.624
Perfect.

00:02:51.657 --> 00:02:54.390
So, is that brandi with a "y" or an "i"?

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:14.924
All right, listen. I got to go.

00:03:14.958 --> 00:03:17.058
Hold that thought. I'll
be right back, okay?

00:03:19.123 --> 00:03:21.757
All right, so, i think i got
something. Oh, yeah, me too.

00:03:21.791 --> 00:03:23.724
I think we need to take
a little shore leave

00:03:23.757 --> 00:03:25.791
For just a little bit.
What do you think, huh?

00:03:25.824 --> 00:03:27.457
I'm so in the door with this one here.

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.891
So, what are we today,
dean? Are we rock stars?

00:03:29.924 --> 00:03:31.223
Are we army rangers?

00:03:31.257 --> 00:03:33.924
We're l.A. Tv scouts looking
for people with special skills.

00:03:35.024 --> 00:03:37.058
But, hey, it's not that far off, right?

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:39.791
By the way, she's got
a friend over there.

00:03:39.824 --> 00:03:41.657
I can probably hook you
up. What do you think?

00:03:41.691 --> 00:03:43.424
Dean, uh, no thanks.
I can get my own dates.

00:03:43.457 --> 00:03:45.524
Yeah, you can, but you don't.

00:03:45.557 --> 00:03:47.591
What is that supposed to mean?

00:03:47.624 --> 00:03:49.324
Nothing. What do you got?

00:03:49.357 --> 00:03:51.891
Mark and ann telesca
of new paltz, new york,

00:03:51.924 --> 00:03:54.991
Were both found dead in their
home just a few days ago.

00:03:55.024 --> 00:03:56.857
Throats were slit, there were no prints,

00:03:56.891 --> 00:03:58.657
No murder weapons, all
- Dean?

00:03:58.691 --> 00:03:59.958
No prints, no murder weapons,

00:03:59.991 --> 00:04:01.958
All doors and windows were
locked from the inside.

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:04.058
Could just be a garden-Variety murder.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.390
You know, not our department.
No, dad says different.

00:04:06.424 --> 00:04:07.457
What do you mean?

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:08.457
Look.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:09.657
Dad noted three murders

00:04:09.691 --> 00:04:11.591
In the same area of upstate new york.

00:04:11.624 --> 00:04:14.157
First one, right here, 1912.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:17.958
The second one in 1945,
and the third in 1970.

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:20.524
The same m.O. As the telescas
- The throats were slit,

00:04:20.557 --> 00:04:22.324
The houses were locked from the inside.

00:04:22.357 --> 00:04:23.891
So much time passed between the murders

00:04:23.924 --> 00:04:25.724
That nobody checked the
pattern except for dad.

00:04:25.757 --> 00:04:27.757
He always kept his eyes
peeled for another one.

00:04:27.791 --> 00:04:29.123
And now we got one. Exactly.

00:04:29.157 --> 00:04:31.357
All right. I'm with you.
It's worth checking out.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.624
We can't pick this up till
first thing, though, right?

00:04:33.657 --> 00:04:35.958
Yeah. Good.

00:04:35.991 --> 00:04:37.457
Dean...

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:38.924
Ladies. Did you miss me?

00:04:38.958 --> 00:04:40.624
I'm just kidding.

00:04:40.657 --> 00:04:43.490
Listen, i talked to my
producer, and it is looking good.

00:04:59.958 --> 00:05:01.857
Oh, man, that's so not cool.

00:05:01.891 --> 00:05:05.357
I just swept the telesca
house with the emf. It's clean.

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:08.024
And last night, while you were...

00:05:08.058 --> 00:05:09.290
Out...

00:05:09.324 --> 00:05:10.624
Oh, good times.

00:05:10.657 --> 00:05:12.290
...i checked the history of the house.

00:05:12.324 --> 00:05:13.924
No hauntings, no violent crimes,

00:05:13.958 --> 00:05:16.457
Nothing strange about the
telescas themselves, either.

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:18.791
So if it's not the people
and it's not the house,

00:05:18.824 --> 00:05:20.390
Then maybe it's the contents -

00:05:20.424 --> 00:05:22.591
A cursed object or
something. House is clean.

00:05:22.624 --> 00:05:23.991
You said that.

00:05:24.024 --> 00:05:25.024
No, i mean it's empty.

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:27.058
No furniture, nothing.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.390
Where's all their stuff?

00:05:57.424 --> 00:06:00.524
Silent auctions, estate sales -

00:06:00.557 --> 00:06:03.190
It's like a garage sale for
w.A.S.P.S, if you ask me.

00:06:03.223 --> 00:06:04.557
Can i help you, gentlemen?

00:06:07.223 --> 00:06:10.090
I'd like some champagne, please.

00:06:10.123 --> 00:06:11.857
He's not a waiter.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:18.424
I'm sam connors.

00:06:18.457 --> 00:06:21.058
This is my brother, dean.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:23.223
We are art dealers with connors limited.

00:06:23.257 --> 00:06:25.190
You're art dealers? That's right.

00:06:25.223 --> 00:06:27.624
I'm daniel blake. This
is my auction house.

00:06:27.657 --> 00:06:30.824
Now, gentlemen, this
is a private showing,

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:33.757
And i don't remember seeing
you on the guest list.

00:06:33.791 --> 00:06:35.090
We're there, chuckles.

00:06:35.123 --> 00:06:37.290
You just need to take another look.

00:06:37.324 --> 00:06:38.724
Oh, finally.

00:06:41.257 --> 00:06:42.524
Cheers.

00:07:00.591 --> 00:07:03.791
A fine example of american
primitive, wouldn't you say?

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:12.691
Well, i'd say it's more
grant wood than grandma moses

00:07:14.324 --> 00:07:15.757
But you knew that.

00:07:15.791 --> 00:07:17.424
You just wanted to see if i did.

00:07:17.457 --> 00:07:19.257
Guilty.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.958
And clumsy. I apologize.

00:07:21.991 --> 00:07:23.924
I'm sarah blake.

00:07:23.958 --> 00:07:26.524
I'm sam.

00:07:26.557 --> 00:07:30.991
This is my...brother, dean.

00:07:31.024 --> 00:07:32.424
Dean. Hmm.

00:07:32.457 --> 00:07:34.090
Can we get you some more mini quiche?

00:07:34.123 --> 00:07:36.657
Mnh-Mnh, i'm good. Thanks.

00:07:36.691 --> 00:07:39.123
So, can i help you with something?

00:07:39.157 --> 00:07:41.490
Yeah, actually.

00:07:41.524 --> 00:07:44.357
What can you tell us
about the telesca estate?

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:46.557
The whole thing's pretty
grisly if you ask me,

00:07:46.591 --> 00:07:48.557
Selling their things this soon.

00:07:48.591 --> 00:07:50.691
But dad's right about one thing -

00:07:50.724 --> 00:07:52.958
Sensationalism brings out the crowds.

00:07:52.991 --> 00:07:55.424
Even the rich ones.

00:07:58.223 --> 00:08:00.290
Is it possible to see the provenances?

00:08:00.324 --> 00:08:04.123
I'm afraid there isn't
any chance of that.

00:08:04.157 --> 00:08:06.123
Why not?

00:08:06.157 --> 00:08:07.724
You're not on the guest list...

00:08:07.757 --> 00:08:09.290
And i think it's time to leave.

00:08:09.324 --> 00:08:11.324
Well, we don't have to be
told twice. Apparently, you do.

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:12.390
Okay, it's all right.

00:08:12.424 --> 00:08:15.290
We don't want any trouble. We'll go.

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:24.457
Dad, that was rude.

00:08:27.357 --> 00:08:29.791
Grant wood, grandma moses
- What?

00:08:29.824 --> 00:08:31.157
Art history course.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.757
It's good for meeting girls.

00:08:32.791 --> 00:08:34.591
It's like i don't even know you.

00:08:51.591 --> 00:08:52.691
Huh.Huh.

00:08:52.724 --> 00:08:54.891
And what was the providence?

00:08:54.924 --> 00:08:56.024
Provenance.

00:08:56.058 --> 00:08:57.490
It's a certificate of origin,

00:08:57.524 --> 00:08:58.857
Like a biography, you know?

00:08:58.891 --> 00:09:01.123
We can use them to track
the history of the pieces,

00:09:01.157 --> 00:09:02.857
See if anything's got a freaky past.

00:09:02.891 --> 00:09:05.223
We're not getting
anything out of chuckles,

00:09:05.257 --> 00:09:06.691
But, uh, sarah... yeah.

00:09:06.724 --> 00:09:08.591
Maybe you can get her
to write it on a napkin.

00:09:08.624 --> 00:09:10.024
Not me.

00:09:10.058 --> 00:09:11.424
Oh, no, no, no, no.

00:09:11.457 --> 00:09:13.123
Pickups are your thing, dean.

00:09:13.157 --> 00:09:15.290
It wasn't my butt she was checking out.

00:09:15.324 --> 00:09:18.624
In other words, you want me
to use her to get information.

00:09:18.657 --> 00:09:20.190
Sometimes you got to
take one for the team.

00:09:20.223 --> 00:09:22.724
Call sarah.

00:09:27.058 --> 00:09:28.490
Nice place.

00:09:28.524 --> 00:09:29.624
Yeah.

00:09:37.991 --> 00:09:39.090
Glad you called.

00:09:40.157 --> 00:09:42.324
Surprised, but glad.

00:09:42.357 --> 00:09:43.390
Yeah?

00:09:43.424 --> 00:09:45.223
Although you seemed to have a hard time

00:09:45.257 --> 00:09:47.624
Getting out the words, "would
you like to have dinner?"

00:09:47.657 --> 00:09:49.724
Yeah.

00:09:49.757 --> 00:09:52.924
I haven't really been
on a date in a while.

00:09:52.958 --> 00:09:54.390
Welcome to the club.

00:09:54.424 --> 00:09:56.857
You're kidding me.

00:09:56.891 --> 00:10:00.657
Man: here we are.

00:10:00.691 --> 00:10:02.290
The wine list.

00:10:15.691 --> 00:10:20.424
I don't know about romeo
here, but i'll have a beer.

00:10:22.724 --> 00:10:23.757
And you?

00:10:23.791 --> 00:10:25.090
I will, too.

00:10:25.123 --> 00:10:26.157
Certainly.

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:28.524
Sam: so, you studied art in school, huh?

00:10:28.557 --> 00:10:29.591
Sarah: it's true.

00:10:29.624 --> 00:10:30.691
I was an artist -

00:10:30.724 --> 00:10:34.657
A terrible, terrible artist.

00:10:34.691 --> 00:10:36.657
That's why i'm in the auction business.

00:10:36.691 --> 00:10:38.190
And you were pre-Law?

00:10:38.223 --> 00:10:39.290
Yeah.

00:10:39.324 --> 00:10:42.290
But you didn't go to
law school. How come?

00:10:42.324 --> 00:10:46.024
Uh, it's a really long
story for another time.

00:10:46.058 --> 00:10:48.657
You're not like any art
dealer i've ever met.

00:10:53.757 --> 00:10:56.058
So...what did you mean when you said

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.724
You hadn't been on a date in a while?

00:10:57.757 --> 00:10:59.490
Trying to make me feel
like i'm not such a loser?

00:10:59.524 --> 00:11:01.223
I'm sure many things, sam.

00:11:01.257 --> 00:11:04.390
I'm also sure "loser" isn't one of them.

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:11.490
It was my mom.

00:11:11.524 --> 00:11:13.757
She died about a year ago.

00:11:13.791 --> 00:11:16.357
Totally unexpected.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:19.824
It really threw me.

00:11:21.524 --> 00:11:27.190
I went into this shell
- A nice, warm, safe shell.

00:11:27.223 --> 00:11:29.991
But lately, i've been thinking...

00:11:30.024 --> 00:11:33.624
It's not what she would
have wanted for me.

00:11:33.657 --> 00:11:35.123
So...

00:11:40.257 --> 00:11:41.557
So, what about you?

00:11:41.591 --> 00:11:44.290
You're a reasonably attractive guy.

00:11:45.958 --> 00:11:47.691
Reasonably.

00:11:47.724 --> 00:11:50.891
Why haven't you been out and about?

00:11:59.123 --> 00:12:02.824
Another long story for another time.

00:12:08.991 --> 00:12:10.857
So, she just handed the
providences over to you?

00:12:10.891 --> 00:12:12.058
Provenances.

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:14.924
Provenances? Yes, we
went back to her place.

00:12:14.958 --> 00:12:17.257
I got a copy of the papers.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:18.757
And?

00:12:18.791 --> 00:12:22.024
And nothing. That's it. I left.

00:12:22.058 --> 00:12:26.424
You didn't have to con her
or do any special favors?

00:12:26.457 --> 00:12:28.457
Would you get your mind
out of the gutter, please?

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:30.991
When this whole thing's done,
we could stick around a bit.

00:12:31.024 --> 00:12:32.757
Why? So you could take her out again.

00:12:32.791 --> 00:12:34.624
It's obvious you're into
her. Even i can see that.

00:12:34.657 --> 00:12:36.924
Hey, all right. I think
i got something here.

00:12:41.157 --> 00:12:42.958
"Portrait of isaiah merchant's family,

00:12:42.991 --> 00:12:44.324
Painted 1910."

00:12:44.357 --> 00:12:46.424
Now compare the names of the
owners with dad's journal.

00:12:50.724 --> 00:12:54.490
"First purchased in 1912 to peter sims."

00:12:54.524 --> 00:12:56.724
Peter sims murdered, 1912.

00:13:00.791 --> 00:13:03.424
Same thing in 1945.

00:13:03.457 --> 00:13:05.958
Oh, same thing in 1970.

00:13:05.991 --> 00:13:07.223
Then stored,

00:13:07.257 --> 00:13:09.591
Until it was donated to a
charity auction last month,

00:13:09.624 --> 00:13:11.490
Where the telescas bought it.

00:13:11.524 --> 00:13:14.190
So, what do you think?
It's haunted or cursed?

00:13:14.223 --> 00:13:16.390
Either way, it's toast.

00:13:38.757 --> 00:13:40.324
Go ahead.

00:14:25.058 --> 00:14:26.424
Ugly-Ass thing.

00:14:26.457 --> 00:14:29.324
If you ask me, we're doing
the art world a favor.

00:14:58.974 --> 00:15:01.240
We got a problem. I
can't find my wallet.

00:15:01.974 --> 00:15:03.741
How's that my problem?

00:15:03.774 --> 00:15:07.108
'Cause i think i dropped it
in the warehouse last night.

00:15:07.141 --> 00:15:08.141
You're kidding, right?

00:15:08.174 --> 00:15:09.874
I mean, it's got my prints, my i.D. -

00:15:09.907 --> 00:15:11.974
Well, my fake i.D.,
anyway, but we got to get it

00:15:12.007 --> 00:15:13.807
Before somebody else finds it. Come on.

00:15:24.074 --> 00:15:26.141
How do you lose your wallet, dean?

00:15:27.907 --> 00:15:29.741
Hey, guys.

00:15:29.774 --> 00:15:32.041
Sarah. Hey.

00:15:32.074 --> 00:15:33.640
What are you doing here?

00:15:33.674 --> 00:15:35.874
Oh...

00:15:35.907 --> 00:15:37.240
We're
- We're leaving town,

00:15:37.273 --> 00:15:39.373
And, you know, we came to say goodbye.

00:15:39.407 --> 00:15:41.208
What are you talking about, sam?

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:44.041
We're sticking around for
at least another day or two.

00:15:44.074 --> 00:15:45.607
Oh, sam, by the way,

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:49.041
I wanted to give you
that 20 bucks i owe you.

00:15:49.074 --> 00:15:52.373
I always forget.

00:15:52.407 --> 00:15:54.474
There you go.

00:15:57.174 --> 00:15:58.974
Well, i'll leave you
two crazy kids alone.

00:15:59.007 --> 00:16:01.607
I got to go do... something...somewhere.

00:16:08.841 --> 00:16:10.741
So...

00:16:10.774 --> 00:16:12.141
I had a good time last night.

00:16:12.174 --> 00:16:14.174
Yeah. Yeah, i did, too.

00:16:14.208 --> 00:16:17.174
Maybe we should do it again sometime?

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:21.741
You know, i'd love to, i really would,

00:16:21.774 --> 00:16:23.574
But dean
- He was just screwing around.

00:16:23.607 --> 00:16:25.841
We really are taking off today.

00:16:25.874 --> 00:16:28.041
Oh. Oh.

00:16:28.074 --> 00:16:29.474
Now that's too bad.

00:16:29.507 --> 00:16:32.307
Oh, my god! What?

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:33.741
The -

00:16:33.774 --> 00:16:35.373
That painting...

00:16:35.407 --> 00:16:37.607
Looks so good.

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.941
If you can call that monstrosity good,

00:16:40.974 --> 00:16:42.707
Then, yeah, i guess.

00:16:42.741 --> 00:16:44.741
Sarah, what do you know
about that painting?

00:16:44.774 --> 00:16:46.974
Not much. Just that it creeps me out.

00:16:47.007 --> 00:16:48.440
We sold it to the telescas

00:16:48.474 --> 00:16:50.440
At a charity auction the
night they were murdered.

00:16:50.474 --> 00:16:52.974
And now you're just gonna sell it again?

00:16:53.007 --> 00:16:55.907
As much as my dad wants
to, no. I won't let him.

00:16:55.941 --> 00:16:57.874
I think it'd be in bad taste.

00:16:57.907 --> 00:16:59.674
Good, yeah. You know what? Don't. Don't.

00:16:59.707 --> 00:17:01.307
Make sure you don't, okay? Why?

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:03.407
Don't tell me you're interested in that.

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:05.273
No, god, no. Not in buying it, no.

00:17:05.307 --> 00:17:07.874
I got to go. I got to
take care of something.

00:17:07.907 --> 00:17:09.440
But, um, i will call you back.

00:17:09.474 --> 00:17:11.007
I will call you. I'll see you later.

00:17:11.041 --> 00:17:13.373
Wait, so you're not leaving tonight?

00:17:13.407 --> 00:17:16.874
No, i guess not. I'll see you.

00:17:18.874 --> 00:17:20.741
Okay.

00:17:22.841 --> 00:17:25.841
I don't understand, dean.
We burned the damn thing.

00:17:25.874 --> 00:17:27.941
Yeah, thank you, captain obvious.

00:17:27.974 --> 00:17:31.907
We just need to figure out
another way to get rid of it.

00:17:31.941 --> 00:17:33.041
Any ideas?

00:17:33.074 --> 00:17:34.307
Okay, all right.

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:36.807
Well, um, in almost all the
lore about haunted paintings,

00:17:36.841 --> 00:17:38.574
It's always the painting's
subject that haunts them.

00:17:38.607 --> 00:17:40.373
Yeah? All right.

00:17:40.407 --> 00:17:42.874
So we need to figure out
everything there is to know

00:17:42.907 --> 00:17:45.640
About that creepy-Ass family
in that creepy-Ass painting.

00:17:45.674 --> 00:17:47.774
What were their names again?

00:17:48.807 --> 00:17:50.108
The isaiah merchant family, right?

00:17:50.141 --> 00:17:51.907
Yeah, that's right.

00:17:51.941 --> 00:17:55.407
I dug up every scrap of
local history i could find.

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:57.440
So, uh, are you boys crime buffs?

00:17:57.474 --> 00:18:00.407
Kind of. Why do you ask?

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:01.774
Well...

00:18:05.373 --> 00:18:07.307
Yes. Yeah, that sounds about right.

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:08.907
The whole family was killed?

00:18:08.941 --> 00:18:11.674
It seems this isaiah, he
slits his kids' throats,

00:18:11.707 --> 00:18:13.707
Then his wife, then himself.

00:18:13.741 --> 00:18:17.507
Now, he was a barber by
trade. Used a straight razor.

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:19.307
Why'd he do it?

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:21.607
Well, let's look.

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:23.640
Uh, "people who knew
him described isaiah

00:18:23.674 --> 00:18:25.607
"As having a stern
and harsh temperament,

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:27.307
And controlled his
family with an iron fist."

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:32.108
Wife, two sons, adopted daughter
- Yeah, yeah.

00:18:32.141 --> 00:18:34.574
There were whispers that the
wife was gonna take the kids

00:18:34.607 --> 00:18:38.474
And leave, which, of course,
you know, in that day and age...

00:18:38.507 --> 00:18:41.607
So instead, old man isaiah,
well, he gave them all a shave.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:42.607
Kkkch!

00:18:44.874 --> 00:18:46.807
Does it say what happened to the bodies?

00:18:46.841 --> 00:18:48.307
They were all cremated.

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:53.041
Anything else? Yeah.

00:18:53.074 --> 00:18:55.974
Actually, i found a
picture of the family.

00:18:56.007 --> 00:18:57.774
It's right here somewhere.

00:18:57.807 --> 00:18:59.707
Right. Here it is.

00:19:07.807 --> 00:19:10.440
Hey, could we get a
copy of this, please?

00:19:10.474 --> 00:19:12.307
Sure.

00:19:16.407 --> 00:19:17.607
Dad...

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:20.807
You promised you wouldn't
sell that painting.

00:19:20.841 --> 00:19:22.674
I know, sweetie, but evelyn's offered

00:19:22.707 --> 00:19:24.208
A persuasive amount of money.

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:27.774
You're shameless, you know that?

00:19:27.807 --> 00:19:30.574
For that kind of money,
i can afford to be.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.240
Sam: i'm telling you,
man. I'm sure of it.

00:19:37.273 --> 00:19:39.774
The painting at the auction
house, dad is looking down.

00:19:39.807 --> 00:19:41.607
The painting here, dad's looking out.

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:42.974
The painting has changed, dean.

00:19:43.007 --> 00:19:45.307
So you think that daddy dearest
is trapped in the painting,

00:19:45.340 --> 00:19:46.974
And he's handing out columbian neckties

00:19:47.007 --> 00:19:49.540
Like he did with his family?
Well, yeah, it seems like it.

00:19:49.574 --> 00:19:51.574
But if his bones are already dusted,

00:19:51.607 --> 00:19:53.407
Then how are we gonna stop him?

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:54.774
Well, if isaiah's position changed,

00:19:54.807 --> 00:19:56.874
Then maybe some other things in
the painting changed, as well.

00:19:56.907 --> 00:19:58.273
It could give us some clues.

00:19:58.307 --> 00:19:59.574
Like a "da vinci code" deal?

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:01.674
I don't know.

00:20:01.707 --> 00:20:04.273
I'm still waiting for
the movie on that one.

00:20:04.307 --> 00:20:06.373
Anyway, we got to get back
in and see that painting,

00:20:06.407 --> 00:20:08.440
Which is a good thing,
because you can get more time

00:20:08.474 --> 00:20:09.707
To crush on your girlfriend.

00:20:09.741 --> 00:20:11.974
Dude...enough already.

00:20:12.007 --> 00:20:14.007
What? "What?" Ever since we got here,

00:20:14.041 --> 00:20:16.108
You've been trying to
pimp me out to sarah.

00:20:16.141 --> 00:20:17.340
Just back off, all right?

00:20:17.373 --> 00:20:18.741
Well, you like her, don't you?

00:20:18.774 --> 00:20:20.440
All right, you like her. She likes you.

00:20:20.474 --> 00:20:22.007
You're both consenting adults.

00:20:22.041 --> 00:20:23.108
What's the point, dean?

00:20:23.141 --> 00:20:24.607
We'll just leave. We always leave.

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:26.373
Well, i'm not talking
about marriage, sam.

00:20:26.407 --> 00:20:28.307
I don't get it. What do
you care if i hook up?

00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:30.208
Maybe you wouldn't be
so cranky all the time.

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:38.340
Seriously, sam, this isn't
about just hooking up, okay?

00:20:38.373 --> 00:20:41.340
I think that this sarah
girl could be good for you.

00:20:43.741 --> 00:20:47.108
And i don't mean any
disrespect, but i'm -

00:20:47.141 --> 00:20:49.074
I'm sure that this is
about jessica, right?

00:20:50.074 --> 00:20:54.874
Now, i don't know what it's like
to lose somebody like that...

00:20:54.907 --> 00:20:56.774
But...

00:20:56.807 --> 00:20:58.807
I would think that she
would want you to be happy.

00:21:01.108 --> 00:21:04.141
God forbid, have fun once in a while.

00:21:04.174 --> 00:21:05.373
Wouldn't she?

00:21:10.041 --> 00:21:11.807
Yeah, i know she would.

00:21:16.807 --> 00:21:22.240
Yeah, you're right. Part
of this is about jessica.

00:21:22.273 --> 00:21:23.640
But not the main part.

00:21:23.674 --> 00:21:25.574
What's it about?

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:31.707
Yeah, all right.

00:21:31.741 --> 00:21:34.707
Well, we still got to see that painting,

00:21:34.741 --> 00:21:38.108
Which means you still
got to call sarah, so...

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:52.074
Sarah, hey. It's sam.

00:21:52.108 --> 00:21:53.941
Hey, hi.

00:21:53.974 --> 00:21:56.208
Good, good, yeah. What about you?

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:58.974
Yeah, good. Good, really good. Smooth.

00:21:59.007 --> 00:22:01.507
So, uh
- So, listen.

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:03.340
Me and my brother were thinking

00:22:03.373 --> 00:22:05.440
That maybe we'd like to come back in

00:22:05.474 --> 00:22:07.273
And look at the painting again.

00:22:07.307 --> 00:22:09.974
I think maybe we are
interested in buying it.

00:22:10.007 --> 00:22:11.174
Wait, what?

00:22:11.208 --> 00:22:14.307
Who'd you sell it to?

00:22:14.340 --> 00:22:16.841
Sarah, i need an address right now.

00:23:01.974 --> 00:23:03.108
Sam, what's happening?

00:23:03.140 --> 00:23:05.240
I told you you shouldn't have come.

00:23:08.774 --> 00:23:10.008
Hello, anybody home?!

00:23:10.041 --> 00:23:12.574
You said evelyn might be in
danger. What kind of danger?

00:23:12.607 --> 00:23:16.474
I can't knock this sucker
down. I got to pick it.

00:23:16.507 --> 00:23:19.041
What are you guys, burglars?

00:23:19.074 --> 00:23:20.374
I wish it was that simple.

00:23:20.407 --> 00:23:22.841
Look, you really should wait in the car.

00:23:22.874 --> 00:23:24.240
Ugh.

00:23:24.273 --> 00:23:25.741
The hell i will. Evelyn's a friend.

00:23:25.774 --> 00:23:26.807
Evelyn?

00:23:26.841 --> 00:23:28.407
Sam: evelyn!

00:23:33.307 --> 00:23:34.540
Evelyn?

00:23:45.074 --> 00:23:47.741
Evelyn?

00:23:47.774 --> 00:23:49.140
It's sarah blake.

00:23:49.173 --> 00:23:50.607
Are you all right?

00:23:50.641 --> 00:23:51.907
Sarah, don't! Sarah!

00:23:58.008 --> 00:24:00.707
Oh, my god! Oh, my god!

00:24:10.108 --> 00:24:12.874
Hey. You all right?

00:24:12.907 --> 00:24:14.307
No, actually.

00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:17.641
I just lied to the cops and told
them i went to evelyn's alone

00:24:17.674 --> 00:24:20.108
And found her like that.

00:24:20.140 --> 00:24:21.273
Thank you. Don't thank me.

00:24:21.307 --> 00:24:22.674
I'm about to call them right back

00:24:22.707 --> 00:24:24.540
If you don't tell me
what the hell is going on.

00:24:24.574 --> 00:24:26.041
Who's killing these people?

00:24:30.173 --> 00:24:31.741
"What."

00:24:31.774 --> 00:24:33.207
What?

00:24:33.240 --> 00:24:34.474
It's not "who."

00:24:34.507 --> 00:24:37.407
It's "what" is killing those people.

00:24:40.340 --> 00:24:42.907
Sarah, you saw that painting move.

00:24:42.941 --> 00:24:45.741
No.

00:24:45.774 --> 00:24:48.440
No, i was
- I was seeing things.

00:24:48.474 --> 00:24:49.807
It's impossible.

00:24:49.841 --> 00:24:51.507
Yeah, well, welcome to our world.

00:24:51.540 --> 00:24:54.774
Sarah, i know this sounds crazy...

00:24:54.807 --> 00:24:57.041
But we think that that
painting is haunted.

00:25:01.440 --> 00:25:02.941
You're joking.

00:25:07.240 --> 00:25:09.741
You're not joking.

00:25:09.774 --> 00:25:12.207
God, the guys i go out with.

00:25:12.240 --> 00:25:13.874
Sarah, think about it.

00:25:13.907 --> 00:25:17.574
Evelyn, the telescas
- They both had the painting.

00:25:17.607 --> 00:25:19.207
And there have been others before that.

00:25:19.240 --> 00:25:20.774
Wherever this thing goes, people die,

00:25:20.807 --> 00:25:23.173
And we're just trying to stop it...

00:25:23.207 --> 00:25:24.607
And that's the truth.

00:25:24.641 --> 00:25:29.507
Well, then, i guess you better show me.

00:25:29.540 --> 00:25:30.540
I'm coming with you.

00:25:30.574 --> 00:25:31.941
What? No.

00:25:31.974 --> 00:25:34.407
Sarah, no. You should just go home.

00:25:34.440 --> 00:25:37.108
This stuff can get dangerous, and

00:25:39.008 --> 00:25:41.008
And i don't want you to get hurt.

00:25:41.041 --> 00:25:42.907
Look, you guys are probably crazy,

00:25:42.941 --> 00:25:44.474
But if you're right about this,

00:25:44.507 --> 00:25:46.507
When me and my dad sold that painting,

00:25:46.540 --> 00:25:48.540
We might have got these people killed.

00:25:48.574 --> 00:25:51.540
I'm not saying i'm not scared,
'cause i am scared as hell,

00:25:51.574 --> 00:25:53.741
But i'm not gonna run and hide, either.

00:25:56.607 --> 00:25:58.474
So are we going or what?

00:25:58.507 --> 00:25:59.674
Sam

00:26:01.707 --> 00:26:03.041
Marry that girl.

00:26:06.041 --> 00:26:09.874
Uh... isn't this a crime scene?

00:26:09.907 --> 00:26:12.474
You've already lied to the
cops. What's another infraction?

00:26:31.607 --> 00:26:35.207
Aren't you worried that it's
gonna, you know, kill us?

00:26:35.240 --> 00:26:37.407
No, it seems to do its thing at night.

00:26:37.440 --> 00:26:38.874
I think we're all right in daylight.

00:26:43.907 --> 00:26:46.140
Sam, check it out.

00:26:46.173 --> 00:26:47.607
The razor
- It's closed in this one,

00:26:47.641 --> 00:26:49.607
But it's open in that one.
What are you guys looking for?

00:26:49.641 --> 00:26:51.374
If the spirit's changing
aspects of the painting,

00:26:51.407 --> 00:26:54.140
Maybe it's doing so for a reason.

00:26:54.173 --> 00:26:58.374
Hey, hey, look at this
- The painting in the painting.

00:27:03.108 --> 00:27:05.774
It looks like a crypt or
a mausoleum or something.

00:27:16.574 --> 00:27:17.807
"Merchant."

00:27:26.540 --> 00:27:29.207
This is the third
boneyard we've checked.

00:27:29.240 --> 00:27:32.474
This ghost is jerking us around.

00:27:32.507 --> 00:27:35.440
So, this is what you
guys do for a living?

00:27:35.474 --> 00:27:38.008
Not exactly.

00:27:38.041 --> 00:27:40.474
We don't get paid.

00:27:40.507 --> 00:27:43.074
Well, mazel tov.

00:27:44.674 --> 00:27:46.807
Over there.

00:28:21.707 --> 00:28:25.874
Okay, that right there is the
creepiest thing i've ever seen.

00:28:25.907 --> 00:28:28.741
It was sort of a tradition at the time.

00:28:28.774 --> 00:28:29.974
Whenever a child died,

00:28:30.008 --> 00:28:32.240
Sometimes they'd preserve
the kid's favorite toy

00:28:32.273 --> 00:28:35.074
In a glass case, put it next
to the headstone in the crypt.

00:28:40.707 --> 00:28:42.474
Notice anything strange here?

00:28:42.507 --> 00:28:43.974
Uh, where do i start?

00:28:44.008 --> 00:28:45.540
No, that's not what i mean.

00:28:45.574 --> 00:28:46.641
Look at the urns.

00:28:48.907 --> 00:28:50.841
Yeah, there are only four.

00:28:50.874 --> 00:28:53.074
Mom and the three kids.

00:28:53.108 --> 00:28:54.807
Daddy dearest isn't here.

00:28:57.074 --> 00:28:58.574
So where is he?

00:28:58.607 --> 00:29:01.207
Sarah: so, what exactly is
your brother doing in there?

00:29:01.240 --> 00:29:03.074
Searching county death certificates,

00:29:03.108 --> 00:29:05.674
Trying to find out what
happened to isaiah's body.

00:29:05.707 --> 00:29:07.307
How'd he even get in the door?

00:29:07.340 --> 00:29:11.741
Lying and subterfuge, mostly.

00:29:13.941 --> 00:29:17.240
You have a, um
- You have an eyelash on your...

00:29:17.273 --> 00:29:19.074
You have it right
- No. Uh, you know what?

00:29:21.140 --> 00:29:22.440
Do you mind if i -

00:29:22.474 --> 00:29:24.841
No. Okay.

00:29:24.874 --> 00:29:26.841
Okay, i got it.

00:29:26.874 --> 00:29:27.941
Make a wish.

00:29:36.173 --> 00:29:37.574
Sam, can i ask you something?

00:29:37.607 --> 00:29:40.240
Yeah, sure. I don't mean to be forward,

00:29:40.273 --> 00:29:44.941
But a girl could wait here forever.

00:29:44.974 --> 00:29:48.974
Is there something here
between us, or am i delusional?

00:29:49.008 --> 00:29:51.041
You're not delusional.

00:29:51.074 --> 00:29:54.140
But there's a "but" coming.

00:29:54.173 --> 00:29:57.240
But...

00:29:57.273 --> 00:29:59.841
I don't think this would be a good idea.

00:30:01.907 --> 00:30:03.041
Can i ask why?

00:30:05.108 --> 00:30:06.273
'Cause i like you.

00:30:08.674 --> 00:30:10.674
Wait. You lost me.

00:30:13.074 --> 00:30:15.807
Look, it's hard to explain.

00:30:15.841 --> 00:30:20.307
It's just that when
people are around me...

00:30:20.340 --> 00:30:22.074
I don't know, they get hurt.

00:30:22.108 --> 00:30:23.140
What do you mean?

00:30:23.173 --> 00:30:26.407
I mean, like, physically hurt.

00:30:26.440 --> 00:30:29.474
With what my brother and i do, it's...

00:30:34.941 --> 00:30:38.240
Sarah...

00:30:38.273 --> 00:30:40.240
I had a girlfriend.

00:30:41.641 --> 00:30:44.041
And she died.

00:30:44.074 --> 00:30:47.807
And my mom died, too.

00:30:47.841 --> 00:30:51.841
I don't know, it's like...

00:30:51.874 --> 00:30:55.074
It's like i'm cursed or something...

00:30:55.108 --> 00:30:56.707
Like death just follows me around.

00:30:56.741 --> 00:30:59.273
Look, i'm not scared of much,

00:30:59.307 --> 00:31:01.774
But if i let myself have
feelings for anybody -

00:31:01.807 --> 00:31:03.674
You're scared they get hurt, too.

00:31:05.574 --> 00:31:10.474
That's very sweet and very archaic.

00:31:10.507 --> 00:31:12.008
Sorry? Look, i'm a big girl, sam.

00:31:12.041 --> 00:31:14.474
It's not your job to
make decisions for me.

00:31:14.507 --> 00:31:16.807
There's always a chance of getting hurt.

00:31:16.841 --> 00:31:18.540
I'm not talking about a broken heart

00:31:18.574 --> 00:31:19.707
And a tub of haagen-Dazs.

00:31:19.741 --> 00:31:20.907
I'm talking about life and death.

00:31:20.941 --> 00:31:22.974
And tomorrow, i could get hit by a bus.

00:31:23.008 --> 00:31:24.108
That's what life is.

00:31:25.173 --> 00:31:28.540
Look, i know losing somebody you love
- It's terrible.

00:31:28.574 --> 00:31:33.108
You shut yourself off.
Believe me, i know.

00:31:33.140 --> 00:31:35.807
But when you shut out pain...

00:31:35.841 --> 00:31:38.041
You shut out everything else, too.

00:31:38.074 --> 00:31:41.641
Sarah, you don't understand.
The pain that i went through...

00:31:41.674 --> 00:31:46.207
I can't go through it again. I can't.

00:31:50.240 --> 00:31:51.874
Am i interrupting something?

00:31:51.907 --> 00:31:53.707
No. Not at all.

00:31:53.741 --> 00:31:55.108
Apparently.

00:31:55.140 --> 00:31:56.941
So, what'd you get? Pay dirt.

00:31:56.974 --> 00:32:00.374
Apparently, the surviving
relatives of the merchant family

00:32:00.407 --> 00:32:02.907
Were so ashamed of isaiah that
they didn't want him interred

00:32:02.941 --> 00:32:05.273
With the family, so they
handed him over to the county.

00:32:05.307 --> 00:32:07.374
The county gave him a pauper's funeral,

00:32:07.407 --> 00:32:08.807
Economy-Style.

00:32:08.841 --> 00:32:11.074
Turns out he wasn't cremated.
He was buried in a pine box.

00:32:11.108 --> 00:32:12.540
<i>So there are bones to burn.</i>

00:32:12.574 --> 00:32:14.974
There are bones to burn.
Tell me you know where.

00:32:28.641 --> 00:32:30.574
You guys seem to be

00:32:30.607 --> 00:32:32.707
Uncomfortably comfortable with this.

00:32:32.741 --> 00:32:37.240
Well...this isn't exactly
the first grave we dug.

00:32:37.273 --> 00:32:41.574
Still think i'm a catch?

00:32:43.008 --> 00:32:45.074
Think i got something.

00:33:11.140 --> 00:33:12.974
Dean: you been a real
pain in the ass, isaiah.

00:33:15.008 --> 00:33:16.641
Good riddance.

00:33:28.140 --> 00:33:29.874
Dean, keep the motor running.

00:33:29.907 --> 00:33:32.707
I thought the painting was harmless now.

00:33:32.741 --> 00:33:35.507
Better safe than sorry.
We're gonna bury the sucker.

00:33:35.540 --> 00:33:36.641
I want to come with you.

00:33:36.674 --> 00:33:38.273
Are you sure?

00:33:38.307 --> 00:33:40.008
Hey, hey, hey.

00:33:40.041 --> 00:33:42.607
I'll stay here. You go make your move.

00:33:42.641 --> 00:33:44.474
S- S-Sam,
i'm serious!

00:34:11.874 --> 00:34:14.173
Uh, sam...

00:34:14.207 --> 00:34:16.941
You're the expert on
all this ghost stuff.

00:34:16.974 --> 00:34:18.374
Is that painting supposed
to look like that?

00:34:20.907 --> 00:34:23.008
Where's the little girl?

00:34:25.540 --> 00:34:26.974
And the razor?

00:34:41.941 --> 00:34:44.641
Dean! Hey, is that you?!

00:34:44.674 --> 00:34:46.140
Dean: sammy, you all right?!

00:34:51.340 --> 00:34:52.941
Tell me you slammed the front door.

00:34:52.974 --> 00:34:54.674
No, it wasn't me. I think
it was the little girl.

00:34:54.707 --> 00:34:56.774
Girl? What girl? Yeah,
she's out of the painting.

00:34:56.807 --> 00:34:58.307
I think it might have
been her all along.

00:34:58.340 --> 00:34:59.674
Wasn't the dad looking down at her?

00:34:59.707 --> 00:35:01.140
Maybe he was trying to warn us.

00:35:01.173 --> 00:35:03.574
Hey, let's recap later.
Just get us out of here.

00:35:03.607 --> 00:35:06.407
I'm trying to pick the lock, and
the door won't budge. Break it down.

00:35:06.440 --> 00:35:09.407
Okay, genius, let me grab my battering
ram! Dean, the damn thing's coming!

00:35:09.440 --> 00:35:11.574
You're gonna have to hold it
off until i figure something out.

00:35:11.607 --> 00:35:13.574
Get some salt or iron.

00:35:16.707 --> 00:35:18.907
What kind of house doesn't have salt?

00:35:18.941 --> 00:35:21.407
Hey, you find any
iron? No, what's it for?

00:35:21.440 --> 00:35:23.307
Iron repels evil spirits,
but it's got to be pure.

00:35:23.340 --> 00:35:25.574
Hurry.

00:35:25.607 --> 00:35:29.173
Uh, dean, give me a
sec. Don't go anywhere.

00:35:29.207 --> 00:35:31.707
Look at a chair. Sometimes the seats...

00:35:50.574 --> 00:35:51.674
Sam!

00:36:09.574 --> 00:36:11.874
That is just so wrong.

00:36:33.273 --> 00:36:36.108
Iron?

00:36:36.140 --> 00:36:37.173
Yeah.

00:36:37.207 --> 00:36:39.540
Sam, are you okay?

00:36:39.574 --> 00:36:40.574
Yeah, for now.

00:36:40.607 --> 00:36:41.974
How we gonna waste her?

00:36:42.008 --> 00:36:43.774
I don't know. She was already cremated.

00:36:43.807 --> 00:36:46.041
There's nothing left to burn.
Well, then, how's she still around?

00:36:46.074 --> 00:36:47.440
There must be something else.

00:36:48.741 --> 00:36:50.240
Sam, wait.

00:36:50.273 --> 00:36:52.440
We used to handle antique
dolls at the auction.

00:36:52.474 --> 00:36:55.540
Well, that's fascinating,
sarah, but important right now?

00:36:55.574 --> 00:36:58.707
Back then, they used to make
the dolls in the kid's image.

00:36:58.741 --> 00:36:59.941
I mean, everything.

00:36:59.974 --> 00:37:02.407
Like, they would use
the kid's real hair.

00:37:02.440 --> 00:37:03.607
Dean?

00:37:03.641 --> 00:37:06.574
Sarah says the doll might
have the girl's hair.

00:37:06.607 --> 00:37:09.574
Human remains
- Same as bones.

00:37:09.607 --> 00:37:11.440
Both: the mausoleum.

00:37:40.207 --> 00:37:41.974
Sam!

00:38:06.974 --> 00:38:07.974
Come on, dean.

00:38:28.207 --> 00:38:30.140
Come on! Come on!

00:39:22.240 --> 00:39:23.474
Sam, you good?

00:39:27.607 --> 00:39:28.674
Not bad.

00:39:47.524 --> 00:39:49.958
This was archived in the county records.

00:39:49.991 --> 00:39:52.524
The merchant's adopted
daughter, melanie.

00:39:52.557 --> 00:39:54.123
Know why she was up for adoption?

00:39:54.157 --> 00:39:57.024
'Cause her real family
was murdered in their beds.

00:39:57.058 --> 00:39:58.290
She killed them?

00:39:58.324 --> 00:40:00.058
Yeah, who would suspect
her? A sweet little girl.

00:40:00.090 --> 00:40:02.290
So then she kills isaiah and his family.

00:40:02.324 --> 00:40:03.791
The old man takes the blame.

00:40:03.824 --> 00:40:06.024
His spirit's been trying
to warn people ever since.

00:40:06.058 --> 00:40:07.724
Where's this one go?

00:40:07.757 --> 00:40:09.357
Take it out back and burn it.

00:40:11.290 --> 00:40:14.757
I'm serious, guys. Thanks.

00:40:17.490 --> 00:40:19.624
So, why'd the girl do it?

00:40:19.657 --> 00:40:21.624
Killing others, killing herself -

00:40:21.657 --> 00:40:23.691
Some people are just born tortured.

00:40:23.724 --> 00:40:26.390
So when they die, their
spirits are just as dark.

00:40:26.424 --> 00:40:28.657
Maybe. I don't really care. It's over.

00:40:28.691 --> 00:40:31.324
We move on.

00:40:33.157 --> 00:40:34.757
I guess this means you're leaving.

00:40:41.524 --> 00:40:45.457
I'll go wait in the car. See you, sarah.

00:40:49.757 --> 00:40:51.924
I'm the one who burned the
doll and destroyed the spirit,

00:40:51.958 --> 00:40:53.157
But don't thank me or anything.

00:40:59.190 --> 00:41:02.524
There are a million things
that i want to say to you,

00:41:02.557 --> 00:41:05.457
But for the life of me,
i can't think of one.

00:41:05.490 --> 00:41:08.390
Yeah, i'll miss you, too.

00:41:08.424 --> 00:41:10.924
You know, there's a
lesson in all of this.

00:41:10.958 --> 00:41:11.958
What's that?

00:41:11.991 --> 00:41:14.591
We all got through this in one piece.

00:41:15.691 --> 00:41:17.290
I didn't get hurt.

00:41:17.324 --> 00:41:19.324
Yeah, i'm glad for that.

00:41:19.357 --> 00:41:22.724
So maybe you're not cursed.

00:41:22.757 --> 00:41:25.223
Maybe...

00:41:28.557 --> 00:41:31.024
Maybe you'll come back and see me.

00:41:34.691 --> 00:41:36.257
I will.

00:42:20.058 --> 00:42:22.691
That's my boy.



00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
